{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 4.5% a year from $70.3 billion in FY2016 to $104.8 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F205], but the path was a step change, not a smooth climb."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Revenue jumped 19.8% in FY2020 and 13.3% in FY2021 [D183][D230], then fell 1.6%, 0.8% and 1.7% in FY2023 through FY2025 [D324][D370][D416]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2020 surge came from a 19.3% comparable sales increase and new stores, with the pandemic shifting category and channel mix [P51][P55]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The recent decline reflects a 2.6% comparable sales decrease in FY2025, driven by a 2.2% traffic decline and a 0.4% lower average transaction [P14]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Merchandise sales were 98.0% of revenue in FY2025 and contributed -2.0pp to that year's decline [D465][D467]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Food & beverage grew 1.3% in FY2025 and added 0.3pp, while apparel fell 4.7% and subtracted 0.7pp [D507][D508][D564][D565]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2023 sales decline came primarily from the Discretionary categories (Apparel & Accessories, Hardlines, Home Furnishings & Decor), partly offset by Frequency categories [P30]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 0.6% a year over the window against 4.5% revenue growth [F207][F205], and in FY2025 operating costs grew 0.4pp faster than revenue [D439]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS compounded at 6.3% against 3.4% net income growth [F210][F208], helped by a 1.3% lower diluted share count in FY2025 [D434]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2025 operating margin of 4.9% sat below the 5.6% window median and well below the 8.4% FY2021 high [F34][D590][D589]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The 0.3pp operating-margin decline in FY2025 came from a 0.3pp cost-of-revenue effect, partly offset by a 0.1pp SG&A benefit [D429][D440][D441]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The gross margin rate fell to 27.9% from 28.2% on the net impact of several items [P12], and the SG&A rate held at 20.6% with a 0.6pp interchange settlement benefit offset by 0.2pp of transformation costs [P11]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2025 net margin of 3.5% sat 1.3pp below the 4.9% operating margin [F54][F34][D629], with a 22.3% effective tax rate [D403]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $6.56 billion was 1.77x net income in FY2025, below the 2.01x window median [F84][F44][D404][D619]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2025 operating cash flow decrease reflects lower net earnings and the net impact of lower accounts payable leverage and inventory purchases [P7]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow fell to $2.84 billion, a 2.7% margin against the 4.5% window median [F104][D401][D596], as capex of $3.73 billion ran at 1.19x D&A [F94][D406]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2025 capex increase primarily reflects increased investment in both new stores and remodels [P5]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Cash of $5.49 billion against long-term debt of $14.4 billion leaves the company in net debt [F144][F194]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The current ratio was 0.94x, in line with the 0.94x window median [F184][D602], and return on average equity of 24.0% was below the 28.6% peer median (n=5) [D415][D617]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks plus dividends of $2.46 billion were 86.8% of free cash flow in FY2025 [D412][D413], with repurchases down to $408 million [X126]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "The diluted share count fell 1.3% in FY2025 [D434], extending a steady reduction from 582.5 million shares in FY2016 [X107]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue declined in FY2023, FY2024 and FY2025, from $109.1 billion to $104.8 billion [R1][F7][F10]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "Three straight down years on a shrinking store base is the central risk, and the FY2025 traffic decline points to demand rather than mix alone [P14]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "The current ratio was 0.94x in FY2025, below 1.0x [R2][F184]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "A sub-1.0x current ratio is normal for this retailer and matches its own median, so it is not a liquidity concern [D602]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "The pack's liquidity and debt figures carry a data break: short-term investments sit inside cash, and the current debt portion sits inside long-term debt for FY2016-FY2018 [R7][R8]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "Net cash and total-debt comparisons across those years are therefore not reliable, and this analysis avoids building conclusions on them."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether the operating margin holds above the 4.9% FY2025 level or slips toward the 3.5% FY2022 low [F34][D588], reported in the FY2026 10-K."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether free cash flow margin recovers toward the 4.5% window median from 2.7% [D401][D596], with capex guided at approximately $5 billion for 2026 [P4]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether revenue growth turns positive from the -1.7% FY2025 rate [D416], reported in the FY2026 10-K."}
  ]}
]}
